course: dictionary
lesson: 9722
title: Sunbathe and the sun
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To sunbathe means to sit or lie in the sunshine, usually to relax or to get a tan. Read the clues around the word. «Ring-tailed lemurs sunbathe in the morning to warm up.» They are not relaxing for fun here: they want to warm up, so sunbathe means sitting or lying in the sun to get warm.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. «Meerkats sunbathe belly to the sun after cold desert nights.» Does "meerkats lie in the sun to warm up after cold nights" make sense? Yes, so your meaning is right.
explain: Sunbathing is also linked to sun safety. Too much sun burns skin, so people use sunscreen, a hat and shade. In Australia and New Zealand, the message is «Slip, Slop, Slap».
fact: Sunbathe means to sit or lie in the sunshine.
fact: People sunbathe to relax or to get a tan.
fact: The verb forms are sunbathe, sunbathes, sunbathed and sunbathing.
fact: Too much sun burns skin and can cause skin cancer later, so people use sunscreen, a hat and shade.
fact: Animals such as lizards also sunbathe, which is called basking, to warm their bodies.
exercise: «They sunbathe on the beach all afternoon.» Which phrase could replace sunbathe without changing the meaning? | swim underwater | sleep in the dark | get soaked in the rain | *lie in the sun
exercise: Meerkats sunbathe after cold desert nights. What does sunbathe mean here? | Hunt for scorpions at night | Dig a hole in the sand to hide | Swim in a cold pool | *Sit or lie in the sunshine to warm up
exercise: Why do people use sunscreen, a hat and shade when they sunbathe? | *To protect their skin from burning | To keep their feet dry | To make them taller | To stop the wind
test: Yesterday we ___ at the pool. | sunbathe | *sunbathed | sunbathing | sunbathes
test: «Lizards sunbathe to warm their bodies.» Why do lizards sunbathe? | *To warm their bodies | To sleep | To clean their scales | To hide from birds
exam: Which sentence shows that the lemurs are lying in the sun to warm up? | The lemurs eat fruit each morning | The lemurs hide in the trees at night | *The lemurs sunbathe each morning to warm up | The lemurs swim in the river each morning
